@crew dlamini-lukas
// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== chat
? endgame:early
- Stayed. Good. One less goodbye. I've enough counting going on.   #warm
? endgame
- Ordinary morning. Up at five, ovens on, porridge right. The galley runs itself. Sort of.   #funny
- Same stool, same drink, same view. You'll get one soon. A stool, I mean.   #funny
- Port Halloran gets rain on Tuesdays. Here we get you on Tuesdays. It'll do.   #warm
- You picked the ship over a desk. Sensible. Desks don't have a galley.

== bye
? endgame
- Night. Breakfast's at seven. It always is. That's the good bit.
